<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur Verdier</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur Verdier was a French merchant and shipowner from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rochelle">La Rochelle</a> whose trading house worked on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a> from the 1860s. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> withdrew its garrisons from the coast after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>, his company kept up the French presence, and he was named French resident in 1878. His firm opened the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> plantation in the colony, at Elima.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arthur-verdier.jpg" alt="Arthur Verdier" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Modjou · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Source_image_au_temps_colonial_de_Arthur_Verdier_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
